  71:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h **** /**
  72:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * @addtogroup XMClib XMC Peripheral Library
  73:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * @{
  74:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  */
  75:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  
  76:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h **** /**
  77:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * @addtogroup VADC
  78:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * @brief Versatile Analog to Digital Converter (VADC) driver for XMC microcontroller family.
  79:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *
  80:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * The XMC microcontroller provides a series of analog input channels connected to a cluster of Ana
  81:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * Converters using the Successive Approximation Register (SAR) principle to convert analog input v
  82:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * to discrete digital values.
  83:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * \if XMC1
  84:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * The XMC1x is based on Sample & Hold converters, where a cluster contains 2 Sample&Hold units whi
  85:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * converter.
  86:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * \endif
  87:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *
  88:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * Each converter of the ADC cluster can operate independent of the others, controlled by a dedicat
  89:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * registers and triggered by a dedicated group request source. The results of each channel can be 
  90:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * dedicated channel-specific result register or in a group-specific result register.<BR>
  91:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *
  92:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * The Versatile Analog to Digital Converter module (VADC) of the XMC comprises a set of converter 
  93:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * can be operated either independently or via a common request source that emulates a background c
  94:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * Each converter block is equipped with a dedicated input multiplexer and dedicated request source
  95:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * which together build separate groups.
  96:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *
  97:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * \if XMC4
  98:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * @image html vadc_overview_xmc4x.png
  99:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * @image latex ../images/vadc_overview_xmc4x.png 
 100:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * \else
 101:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * @image html vadc_overview_xmc1x.png
 102:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * @image latex ../images/vadc_overview_xmc1x.png
 103:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * \endif
 104:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *
 105:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * The VADC LLD is split into GLOBAL and GROUP related APIs.<BR>
 106:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * <B>GLOBAL: </B><BR>
 107:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * <UL>
 108:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * <LI>Global APIs act on the entire ADC module. Configures global configuration registers</LI>
 109:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * <LI>Allows configuration of the background request source of the VADC.</LI>
 110:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * <LI>The clock related configurations for the VADC module are configured in the Global APIs/</LI>
 111:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * <LI>The Global API names are prefixed by the \b XMC_VADC_GLOBAL_ and they accept ::XMC_VADC_GLOB
 112:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *     one of its arguments.</LI>
 113:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * <LI>Configures the background request source of the VADC. The APIs which act on the background r
 114:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *     are prefixed by \b XMC_VADC_GLOBAL_Background</LI>
 115:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * <LI>Configures the sample and hold unit of the VADC. The APIs which act on the SHS related regis
 116:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *     are prefixed by \b XMC_VADC_GLOBAL_SHS_</LI>
 117:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * </UL><BR>
 118:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *
 119:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * <B>GROUP: </B><BR>
 120:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * <UL>
 121:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * <LI>Group APIs act on a VADC group. Configures the group configuration registers</LI>
 122:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * <LI>Configures the queue request source of the VADC. The APIs which act on the queue related reg
 123:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *     are prefixed by \b XMC_VADC_GROUP_Queue</LI>
 124:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * <LI>Configures the scan request source of the VADC. The APIs which act on the scan related regis
 125:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *     are prefixed by \b XMC_VADC_GROUP_Scan</LI>
 126:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * <LI>Configuration of the channels of each group are done by the API which have a prefix as
 127:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *     \b XMC_VADC_GROUP_Channel.</LI>
 128:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * <LI>The Group API names are prefixed by the \b XMC_VADC_GROUP_ and they accept ::XMC_VADC_GROUP_
 129:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *     one of its arguments.</LI>
 130:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * </UL><BR>
 131:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * @{
 132:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  */
 133:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  
