2499:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * Select Gating signal for scan request source.<BR>\n
2500:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * Passage of the trigger input to the request source can be controlled via a gating signal. Any on
2501:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * lines can be chosen as a gating signal. Trigger signal can be given to the scan request source o
2502:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * when the gating signal's active level is detected. Additionally the GxASMR.ENGT has to be config
2503:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * the gating signal's active level. A call to this API would configure the register bit field GxAS
2504:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *
