2960:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * <b>Details of function</b><br>
2961:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * Selects the gating mode of background request source.<BR>\n
2962:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * Passage of the trigger input to the request source can be controlled via a gating signal.
2963:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * This API determines how the gating signal behaves, either active low or active high.
2964:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * If gating signal needs to ignored XMC_VADC_GATEMODE_IGNORE should be used as the \a mode_sel.
