3367:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *
3368:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * \par<b>Description:</b><br>
3369:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * Select Trigger signal edge for queue request source.<BR>\n
3370:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * A queue request source will raise conversion request only if there were either a request from ap
3371:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * occurrence of a hardware trigger. This API selects one of the 4 trigger edges. This is
3372:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * needed when a hardware trigger is needed for the conversion of the queue request source.
3373:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * Refer to the reference manual to determine the signal that needs to be connected.
3374:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * A call to this API would configure the register bit field GxQCTRL0.XTMODE.
3375:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *
