3388:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * Select Gating signal for queue request source.<BR>\n
3389:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * Passage of the trigger input to the request source can be controlled via a gating signal. Any on
3390:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * lines can be chosen as a gating signal. Trigger signal can be given to the queue request source 
3391:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * when the gating signal's active level is detected. Additionally the GxQMR0.ENGT has to be config
3392:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * the gating signal's active level. A call to this API would configure the register bit field GxQC
3393:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *
