3405:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * <b>Details of function</b><br>
3406:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * Selects the gating mode of queue request source.<BR>\n
3407:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * Passage of the trigger input to the request source can be controlled via a gating signal.
3408:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * This API determines how the gating signal behaves, either active low or active high.
3409:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * If gating signal needs to ignored XMC_VADC_GATEMODE_IGNORE should be used as the \a mode_sel.
3410:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * A call to this API would configure the register bit field GxQMR0.ENGT.
3411:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  *
3412:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_vadc.h ****  * \par<b>Related APIs:</b><BR>
